cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic research or coursework, please cite it as below."
title: "neutron-diffusion-reactor-simulator: A Scientific 1D Neutron Diffusion Eigenvalue Solver and Reactor Physics Analysis Framework"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-07
authors:
  - family-names: "Mohammadrezaei"
    given-names: "Arash"
    email: "arashrezaii28@gmail.com"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Arashsyberbrother/neutron-diffusion-reactor-simulator"
url: "https://github.com/Arashsyberbrother/neutron-diffusion-reactor-simulator"
abstract: >-
  A modular, research-oriented computational reactor-physics framework solving the
  steady-state, one-energy-group neutron diffusion eigenvalue problem for both
  homogeneous and multi-region heterogeneous reflected reactor cores in 1D slab
  geometry. Features conservative second-order finite-difference discretization,
  harmonic interface diffusion coefficients, Thomas algorithm (TDMA), power
  iteration, and numerical critical fuel sizing.
keywords:
  - "nuclear engineering"
  - "reactor physics"
  - "neutron diffusion"
  - "power iteration"
  - "eigenvalue problem"
  - "finite differences"
  - "scientific computing"
